// The attacks and the block. The moves for getting around are in movement_moves.hor.
// A character lists the files its moves come from in characters.hor, a move in a later file replaces the one of the same name from an earlier one.
//
// What a move can have:
//   input             the button that starts it. "DPadLeft | DPadRight" is either of them, "A + B" is both together.
//                     The buttons are A, B, X, Y, DPadUp, DPadDown, DPadLeft, DPadRight, LeftBumper, RightBumper, LeftTrigger and RightTrigger.
//                     Which physical button each one sits on is up to the bindings of the player. A move without an input can only be rerouted to.
//   trigger           how the input has to be entered. "held" (for as long as it is), "pressed" (once per press) or "double_tap".
//   priority          the order the inputs are matched in, lowest goes first. A move that needs more than another one has to come before it
//                     (double tap left before left).
//   stances           the stances it can be started from, "standing | crouching | jumping | falling".
//   damage            how much health a hit takes, out of 100.
//   knockback         the shove whoever gets hit is given, vec(away from the attacker, up). Anything with an up part is a launcher.
//   hitstun           how long whoever gets hit loses the controls for, in frames of this move's own animation.
//                     Leave it out and it is worked out from the startup of the move, see the bottom of this comment.
//   cancellable       whether the move can be cancelled into another one at all. Its phases say from which frame.
//   steering          whether the player can walk during the move.
//   turning           whether the player can turn around during the move, the same as steering if it doesn't say.
//   status            what the player is while the move lasts. "attacking", "blocking" (hits from the front bounce off and the player
//                     can't turn around) or "invulnerable" (i-frames, hits go straight through).
//   stance            the stance the move puts the player in, and stance_after the one it leaves them in.
//   warns             whether the opponent gets a heads up that the move is coming (the dummy uses it to block). Moves that do damage warn unless they say no.
//   repeat            a condition (see below) under which the move starts over after its last phase.
//   stance_reroutes   another move to do instead, by the stance the player is in when the input comes (kick in the air is a jump kick).
//   finish_reroutes   the move to carry on with once this one is over, by the stance the player is in by then. Without one they go back to "idle".
//   phases            what the move actually does, see below.
//
// The phases of a move play one after the other in the order they are written. What a phase can have:
//   animation         the animation to play, out of the character's sprite definition. Without one the animation of the phase before carries on.
//   frames            how many frames the phase lasts, as long as its animation if it doesn't say.
//   hit               the frame the hit comes out on, counted from 0. Everything before it is startup and everything after it is recovery.
//   cancel            the frame from which the move can be cancelled into another one.
//   commit            the frame from which the player is committed and can't cancel any more.
//   status            a status (see above) the player only takes on during this phase, from the frame status_frame says (0 if it doesn't).
//                     It lasts until the move is over.
//   loop_while        a condition. The phase starts over for as long as it holds and ends the frame it stops holding.
//   until             a condition. The phase ends the frame it starts holding.
//   impulse           a shove the player gets as the phase starts, vec(the way they are facing, up).
//   effect            a bit of eye candy, "jump", "roll" or "haze". effect_frames is how many frames it keeps coming for (1 if it doesn't say, 0 for all of them).
//
// The conditions are "held" (the input of the move is), "hitstun", "jumping" (on the way up), "falling" and "always".
//
// Four names mean something to the game. "idle" is what a player does when they do nothing (and has to be there),
// "hit_stun" is what they are put in while they are in hitstun, "knocked_out" is where they stay once their health is gone
// (without one they stay in "hit_stun"), and "heavy_land" is what a long fall ends in if there is one.
//
// How hits work (the numbers behind all of this are in Combat/CombatRules.cs):
//   - Every hit puts the victim in hitstun. They are stuck in "hit_stun" and can't do anything until it runs out.
//   - A fast move is a little minus on hit, meaning the victim can act before the attacker can. Mash a jab at them and they can jab you first.
//   - The longer the startup of a move the more plus it is on hit. From some point the attacker recovers first with time to spare,
//     which is the window to link a fast move after it. That is a combo.
//   - A hit on somebody who is already in hitstun doesn't cut their hitstun short, so a jab in the middle of a long hitstun leaves the long one standing.
//   - Somebody who is in hitstun and in the air (a launcher put them there) can be juggled. Every hit adds a little hitstun, less each time.
//   - A hit that catches somebody in the startup of their own attack is a counter hit. More hitstun, more damage.
//   - A hit that catches somebody in the recovery of their own attack is a punish. Same as a normal hit, but the HUD calls them out for it.
//   - Blocking only covers the front, and you can't turn around while you are blocking.

let moves = {
    block: {
        input: "RightBumper",
        trigger: "held",
        priority: 40,
        stances: "standing | crouching",
        cancellable: true,
        steering: false,
        phases: {
            raise: { animation: "block_start", cancel: 0, commit: 3, status: "blocking", status_frame: 2 },
            hold: { animation: "block_loop", loop_while: "held", commit: 0 }
        }
    },

    hit_stun: {
        stances: "standing | crouching | jumping | falling",
        cancellable: false,
        steering: false,
        finish_reroutes: {
            jumping: "fall",
            falling: "fall"
        },
        phases: {
            dazed: { animation: "hard_landing", frames: 1, loop_while: "hitstun", effect: "haze", effect_frames: 0 }
        }
    },

    knocked_out: {
        stances: "standing | crouching | jumping | falling",
        cancellable: false,
        steering: false,
        phases: {
            drop: { animation: "knocked_out" },
            down: { frames: 1, loop_while: "always" }
        }
    },

    kick_left: {
        input: "A",
        trigger: "pressed",
        priority: 20,
        stances: "standing | falling | jumping | crouching",
        damage: 5,
        cancellable: false,
        status: "attacking",
        stance_reroutes: {
            jumping: "jump_kick",
            falling: "jump_kick"
        },
        phases: {
            swing: { animation: "kick", hit: 3 }
        }
    },

    kick_right: {
        input: "B",
        trigger: "pressed",
        priority: 30,
        stances: "standing | falling | jumping | crouching",
        damage: 5,
        cancellable: false,
        status: "attacking",
        stance_reroutes: {
            jumping: "jump_kick",
            falling: "jump_kick"
        },
        phases: {
            swing: { animation: "kick", hit: 3 }
        }
    },

    punch_left: {
        input: "X",
        trigger: "pressed",
        priority: 24,
        stances: "standing | crouching",
        damage: 3,
        cancellable: false,
        status: "attacking",
        phases: {
            swing: { animation: "punch", hit: 2 }
        }
    },

    punch_right: {
        input: "Y",
        trigger: "pressed",
        priority: 34,
        stances: "standing | crouching",
        damage: 3,
        cancellable: false,
        status: "attacking",
        phases: {
            swing: { animation: "punch", hit: 2 }
        }
    },

    jump_kick: {
        stances: "jumping | falling",
        damage: 8,
        knockback: vec(900, 1900),
        hitstun: 12,
        cancellable: false,
        status: "attacking",
        finish_reroutes: {
            standing: "idle",
            falling: "fall"
        },
        phases: {
            swing: { animation: "jump_kick", hit: 4 }
        }
    }
}